# mydash credentials
#
# Weather (Open-Meteo) and news (Noozra) need no API keys.
# Markets (Alpaca) need free credentials: https://alpaca.markets/
# Paper-trading keys work fine for market data.
#
# mydash reads credentials from, highest precedence first:
#   1. real environment variables
#   2. the file named by MYDASH_ENV_FILE
#   3. a .env beside (or above) the directory you run from  <- this file
#   4. .env in the mydash data directory                    <- works anywhere
#
# For a global install, use option 4. Run:
#     mydash config env --create
# which writes a fillable copy of this file to the right place, then:
#     mydash config env
# to see exactly where mydash is looking.
#
# Never commit a filled-in .env.

STOCK_ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=your_alpaca_key_id
STOCK_ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=your_alpaca_secret
